  <h1>About Richlytic</h1>
  <p>Richlytic covers celebrity and public figure net worth with a simple standard: every figure is sourced, every claim is checked against multiple independent reports, and every estimate is presented as exactly that — an estimate, not a confirmed fact.</p>
  <p>We don't inflate numbers for clicks, and we don't present rumors as reporting. Where sources disagree, we say so and explain why.</p>
  <h2>Our Standard</h2>
  <p>Every article on Richlytic is cross-referenced against public business records, court filings, press coverage, and other independently verifiable sources before publication. Personal photos of the individuals we cover are only used with proper rights clearance; where we don't have that, we use clearly labeled illustrative imagery instead.</p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>Richlytic publishes sourced, fact-checked net worth profiles for celebrities and public figures — covering their career, income sources, and the documented facts behind the estimates, not just a headline number.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Every profile starts with research across public records, court filings, and press coverage, followed by a clear breakdown of what's confirmed versus estimated, so readers know exactly where a number comes from.</p>

